WEBVTT

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:35.000
Bism Allah Arrahman Arraheem. In the name of God, Most Gracious, Most Merciful.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:40.000
Islam actually began with the first man, the first human being, Adam. He was the

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:44.000
first messenger of God. He brought to his children, and grandchildren,

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:51.000
the message of worshiping God alone. And this is Islam, submitting to God,

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:57.000
worshiping God alone. A series of messengers after Adam

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:03.000
brought the same message, worship God alone. The first commandment in the Bible,

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:09.000
the message of Moses, the message of Jesus, the messages of all the prophets of

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:14.000
Israel, David, Solomon, and so on, is one and the same, the first commandment,

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:19.000
worship God with all your heart, all your body, and all your soul. Worship

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:24.000
God alone. The Quran states very clearly that the religion as far as God is

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:30.000
concerned is Islam. So, there is only one religion as far as God is concerned.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:35.000
If you want to be more specific, the original prophet of Islam is Abraham

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:41.000
because he brought all the religious practices in Islam. And we see this

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:50.000
throughout the Quran. For example, in Sura 21, verse 73 tells us

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:56.000
that Abraham was the original source of... of course, God is the original source

00:01:56.000 --> 00:02:02.000
of everything, but Abraham delivered to us the Salat prayer, the contact prayers, and the

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:10.000
Zakat charity. This is in Sura 21 verse 73. And we see this also with the

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:15.000
fasting, the Hajj pilgrimage. All the practices of Islam came to us through

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:21.000
the prophet Abraham. The prophet Muhammad contributed the message, the

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:23.000
scripture of Islam which is the Quran.

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:33.000
Abraham was the original prophet of Islam.

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:41.000
All religious duties in Islam came to us through Abraham.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:49.000
All religious duties in Islam came to us through Abraham.

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:54.000
The prophet Muhammad contributed the message, the scripture of Islam, which is the

00:02:54.000 --> 00:03:00.000
Quran. God revealed the Quran to us through the Prophet Muhammad. The Prophet

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:08.000
Muhammad was born in the year 570 AD. And when he was 40 years of age, he was

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:16.000
appointed God's final prophet. Prophet means he brought a new

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:21.000
scripture, the final edition of God's message to the world and that is the

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:26.000
Quran. The Quran was given to the prophet

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:32.000
Muhammad in one night, as we see in the Quran in many many verses, in Sura 17

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:40.000
verse 1, in Sura 44 verse 3, and in Sura 97.

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:49.000
The release of the Quran from Muhammad's soul to his mouth and his hand was done

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:55.000
over a period of 23 years from his age of 40 to the age of 63. He died

00:03:55.000 --> 00:04:02.000
at the age of 63. So, over a period of 23 years, the Quran was being released

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:09.000
after being placed in Muhammad's heart on the night of power - in Arabic لَيْلَةِ ٱلْقَدْرِ

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:14.000
The purpose of releasing the Quran over

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:21.000
23-year period is to help the Prophet and the believers, at the time, to

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:26.000
memorize the Quran as it was being released. And this is stated in the Quran.

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:32.000
In the Quran it says (25:32) لِنُثَبِّتَ بِهِۦ فُؤَادَكَ to fix it in your memory.

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:38.000
So, the release was very slowly, very gradually, and it took 23 years.

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:56.000
Prophet Muhammad's role was to deliver God's final message, the Quran.

00:04:58.000 --> 00:05:04.000
God created the universe and created the human race and out of His mercy, He sent

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:10.000
messengers and books to tell us about Him. All these messengers and all the

00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:15.000
books that God sent to us preach one and the same religion.

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:21.000
The first messenger was Adam himself, the father of all humanity. After him, came

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:27.000
messengers like Noah, Jesus, Moses, Muhammad. Muhammad was the last prophet bringing

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:33.000
the last scripture, the Quran. And in the Quran, we find everything we need,

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:41.000
all the duties, obligations, commandments, prohibitions in Islam. Quran is the

00:05:41.000 --> 00:05:47.000
final scripture. It is the completion of the message. Because the previous

00:05:47.000 --> 00:05:52.000
scriptures were suited for that stage of human development. The Quran came to

00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:59.000
complete the picture and now we have the final, the complete religion, Islam.

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:05.000
The Quran is all you need. In fact, because God said that the Quran is complete,

00:06:05.000 --> 00:06:11.000
perfect, and fully detailed, if you go to any other source, you will be disobeying

00:06:11.000 --> 00:06:15.000
God and disobeying the messenger of God, Muhammad who brought this Quran out of

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:18.000
his mouth. God brought to us the Quran out of

00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:23.000
Muhammad's mouth. And you will be disobeying God and disobeying Muhammad

00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:28.000
if you follow any other sources besides the Quran. And specifically I mean sources

00:06:28.000 --> 00:06:35.000
like Hadith, Sunnah, and all the other books and things that the traditions and

00:06:35.000 --> 00:06:40.000
the customs invented. If you go to any source besides the Quran, you will be

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:46.000
disobeying God. Because clearly God says in Sura number 6, verse

00:06:46.000 --> 00:06:51.000
114, for example, that the Quran is fully detailed. You don't need anything

00:06:51.000 --> 00:06:57.000
else. God says in verse 19 of Sura number 6 that the Quran is what was given to

00:06:57.000 --> 00:07:03.000
Muhammad to deliver to the world, and it is the only source for religious guidance

00:07:03.000 --> 00:07:08.000
and religious education. The Quran tells us exactly what the

00:07:08.000 --> 00:07:13.000
essentials of Islam are, and they are... Very quickly, I'm gonna go into details of

00:07:13.000 --> 00:07:20.000
these later on. Number one: to believe in God alone. You do not have any other idols.

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:26.000
You are devoted to God alone, and this is represented by the SHAHADA, the first

00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:31.000
so-called pillar of Islam. Let us go along with that idea. The first pillar

00:07:31.000 --> 00:07:37.000
of Islam is the SHAHADA, and the SHAHADA is stated in the Quran in Sura number 3

00:07:37.000 --> 00:07:40.000
verse 81.

00:07:41.000 --> 00:07:50.000
Excuse me, it's verse 18. Sura 3, verse 18. It says شَهِدَ ٱللَّهُ means God bears

00:07:50.000 --> 00:07:56.000
witness, أَنَّهُۥ لَآ إِلَـٰهَ إِلَّا هُوَ that there is no god except He.

00:07:56.000 --> 00:08:01.000
And also the angels and those who possess knowledge will make this SHAHADA,

00:08:01.000 --> 00:08:09.000
which is La Elaha Ella Allah or Ash-hadu Alla Elaha Ella Allah. This is the first

00:08:09.000 --> 00:08:15.000
pillar in Islam. Sura number 3, verse number 18.

00:08:15.000 --> 00:08:21.000
The SHAHADA, the first pillar of Islam is La Elaha Ella Allah. If you want to make it

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:27.000
complete, then you say Ash-hadu Alla Elaha Ella Allah. I bear witness that

00:08:27.000 --> 00:08:33.000
there is no god except Allah, the one God. Now, don't add anything else.

00:08:33.000 --> 00:08:41.000
Some people, who imitate old inventions and old traditions, will say

00:08:41.000 --> 00:08:45.000
Ash-hadu Alla Elaha Ella Allah and then they make another SHAHADA that Muhammad is a messenger of

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:50.000
God. We know that Muhammad is a messenger of God, but if you inject this

00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:54.000
in the SHAHADA, this ruins everything, because now you don't have God ALONE.

00:08:54.000 --> 00:09:00.000
You put an idol, Muhammad, next to God. And this is, by the way, is a very strong

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:05.000
prohibition in the Quran that you put any other name besides the name of Allah,

00:09:05.000 --> 00:09:12.000
the name of God. We find this in Sura number 39 verse 45.

00:09:12.000 --> 00:09:16.000
You must say, you must devote yourself to God ALONE. You do not idolize

00:09:16.000 --> 00:09:22.000
Muhammad and put him next to God. This will be going against God and against Muhammad.

00:09:22.000 --> 00:09:27.000
So, the first pillar of Islam is SHAHADA La Elaha Ella Allah.

00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:34.000
The first pillar of Islam is worshiping God ALONE.

00:09:34.000 --> 00:09:41.000
This is expressed by bearing witness that there is no god except the One GOD.

00:09:44.000 --> 00:09:54.000
Verse 18 of Sura 3 teaches the correct statement: There is no god except the one God (La Elaha Ella Allah)

00:09:57.000 --> 00:010:06.000
So, the first pillar of Islam is SHAHADA La Elaha Ella Allah. The second pillar is observing five

00:010:06.000 --> 00:010:13.000
contact prayers every day. This is the food for your soul. This is a favor that God

00:010:13.000 --> 00:010:20.000
is doing for you. You're not doing it for God. And the five contact prayers begin

00:010:20.000 --> 00:010:25.000
before sunrise. You must get up before sunrise in order to feed your

00:010:25.000 --> 00:010:30.000
soul, give you soul breakfast. Your body will be lazy and will not

00:010:30.000 --> 00:010:37.000
want to get out of bed before sunrise. But for your sake, get out of bed before

00:010:37.000 --> 00:010:42.000
sunrise and do the Morning contact prayer, whereby you contact your creator

00:010:42.000 --> 00:010:48.000
and feed your soul. The second prayer... by the way, the details

00:010:48.000 --> 00:010:53.000
of the prayers are given on another videotape that we call Principles of

00:010:53.000 --> 00:010:59.000
Muslim prayer. So, be sure you order that tape and see how the contact prayers are

00:010:59.000 --> 00:011:04.000
performed, the correct way, not the traditional innovations that we see in

00:011:04.000 --> 00:011:10.000
the Muslim world. The second prayer is the Noon prayer.

00:011:10.000 --> 00:011:16.000
And it begins as soon as the sun declines from the highest spot in the sky. That is

00:011:16.000 --> 00:011:21.000
the Noon prayer, consists of four units. The Morning prayer is two units. The

00:011:21.000 --> 00:011:29.000
Noon contact prayer is four units. The Afternoon contact is done about three or

00:011:29.000 --> 00:011:33.000
four hours after the noon prayer in the mid afternoon.

00:011:33.000 --> 00:011:40.000
And the fourth contact prayer is the Sunset prayer or Maghrib. And it is done

00:011:40.000 --> 00:011:46.000
immediately after sunset. And the final contact prayer, the Night prayer, must be

00:011:46.000 --> 00:011:53.000
done about two hours after sunset. So, these are the five contact prayers

00:011:53.000 --> 00:011:57.000
and they represent the second pillar of Islam.

00:011:59.000 --> 00:012:06.000
The second pillar of Islam is the Contact Prayers [Specified actions and words]

00:012:06.000 --> 00:012:16.000
There are 5 Contact Prayers per day, Morning, Noon, Afternoon, Sunset, and the Night Contact.

00:012:16.000 --> 00:012:26.000
These are the daily meals for the soul to nourish the real person [That's you].

00:012:30.000 --> 00:012:37.000
The third pillar of Islam is fasting, in Arabic, SIYAM.

00:012:37.000 --> 00:012:45.000
God commands us to fast during one month of the year, and it is the ninth

00:012:45.000 --> 00:012:52.000
month of the lunar calendar. Now, I'm smiling because there is a

00:012:52.000 --> 00:012:59.000
tremendous test in this system, where the lunar year is shorter than the solar year,

00:012:59.000 --> 00:013:05.000
and this makes the month of Ramadan move about 10 to 15 days every year.

00:013:05.000 --> 00:013:09.000
So, it comes in the winter sometimes when the day is nice and short and fasting is

00:013:09.000 --> 00:013:14.000
very easy, and moves to the summer where the days are very long, 16 hours or more

00:013:14.000 --> 00:013:20.000
sometimes, and the day is hot and you can't eat or drink during this long

00:013:20.000 --> 00:013:24.000
period. And a lot of people will drop out. They will... they will not fast even though

00:013:24.000 --> 00:013:31.000
nobody dies by not eating or drinking for 24 hours. But some people

00:013:31.000 --> 00:013:37.000
will drop out and you can see that the system is designed to show who will fast

00:013:37.000 --> 00:013:42.000
and would obey God's commandment, no matter how long the day is.

00:013:42.000 --> 00:013:49.000
This changing of the day from short and cold to long and hot days will show

00:013:49.000 --> 00:013:54.000
us who are the dropouts, who will fast only if the day is short and nice and

00:013:54.000 --> 00:014:00.000
cold. So, this is the second pillar of Islam, fasting during the month of

00:014:00.000 --> 00:014:04.000
Ramadan, the ninth month of the Islamic calendar.

00:014:04.000 --> 00:014:14.000
The third pillar of Islam is Fasting during one month [Ramadan].

00:014:14.000 --> 00:014:27.000
From dawn to sunset, Muslims do not eat or drink or have any sexual activity [during Ramadan]

00:014:28.000 --> 00:014:35.000
As you see, the fasting of Ramadan is also designed to tame the wild horse,

00:014:35.000 --> 00:014:38.000
your body. See, your body wants to eat and drink,

00:014:38.000 --> 00:014:44.000
and you, the real person or the soul, dictates on the body saying no, you're

00:014:44.000 --> 00:014:49.000
not going to eat or drink until sunset. Because the fasting consists of not

00:014:49.000 --> 00:014:56.000
eating or drinking or engaging in intercourse, sexual intercourse from dawn

00:014:56.000 --> 00:015:03.000
to sunset. Dawn means about two hours before sunrise to sunset, no eating, no

00:015:03.000 --> 00:015:10.000
drinking, no sex. And this is control of your wild horse.

00:015:10.000 --> 00:015:18.000
You are taming the wild horse, your body. And you can see that God is training you,

00:015:18.000 --> 00:015:23.000
is teaching you to be a person of a strong will,

00:015:23.000 --> 00:015:29.000
and preparing you for the eternal life of the Hereafter, the real life.

00:015:29.000 --> 00:015:36.000
Because in the real life that comes after this life, God wants the people who are strong,

00:015:36.000 --> 00:015:42.000
who practice and exercise and know how to control themselves, I mean, their

00:015:42.000 --> 00:015:48.000
their bodies. This also causes your soul to feed, grow and develop.

00:015:49.000 --> 00:015:59.000
Fasting makes you the boss, not your body ... The soul commands the body to control itself.

00:015:59.000 --> 00:016:08.000
Fasting prepares us for a position of prominence and leadership in the real life [Hereafter].

00:016:12.000 --> 00:016:20.000
The fourth pillar of Islam is charity, in Arabic, ZAKAT. There is an obligatory

00:016:20.000 --> 00:016:26.000
charity where you sit down and you calculate exactly what you possess, what

00:016:26.000 --> 00:016:29.000
your possessions are, and you give away a portion,

00:016:29.000 --> 00:016:34.000
a fixed portion of your net worth. You do this once a year.

00:016:34.000 --> 00:016:39.000
You pick out a specific day in the year, the last day of Ramadan, the first day of Ramadan,

00:016:39.000 --> 00:016:44.000
or the first day of January, one day, one fixed day in the year.

00:016:44.000 --> 00:016:48.000
And you sit down on that day and you calculate how much you are worth.

00:016:48.000 --> 00:016:53.000
This means you add up the market value of your house, your car, your clothes,

00:016:53.000 --> 00:016:58.000
anything that you posses if you sell it all today. How much will it be worth?

00:016:58.000 --> 00:017:05.000
The fair market value, not the new... the price of the new thing, no, the present

00:017:05.000 --> 00:017:10.000
market value of everything you posses. And then you give away 2.5% of that.

00:017:10.000 --> 00:017:13.000
See? It's a small percentage. And you do it once a year.

00:017:13.000 --> 00:017:16.000
And it goes to specific people.

00:017:16.000 --> 00:017:21.000
The Quran lists them in this priority: first your parents.

00:017:21.000 --> 00:017:27.000
If your parents are rich... and these are the recipients of your

00:017:27.000 --> 00:017:34.000
charity. If your parents are rich, the second in the list are you relatives.

00:017:34.000 --> 00:017:39.000
You give this 2.5%, you give it to your relatives. If they're all rich,

00:017:39.000 --> 00:017:46.000
then you find some orphans, people who do not have support, parental support, a father

00:017:46.000 --> 00:017:51.000
support or something. And you give this charity to them.

00:017:51.000 --> 00:017:58.000
After the orphans, you give to the alien, somebody who's traveling and is

00:017:58.000 --> 00:018:02.000
stranded and doesn't have the money or the bus fare to go to his home town,

00:018:02.000 --> 00:018:07.000
you help that person. So, the order in the Quran is: the parents, the relatives,

00:018:07.000 --> 00:018:13.000
the orphans, the traveling alien, the poor the beggars and so on. So, there is a

00:018:13.000 --> 00:018:18.000
specific order for giving these charities. However, there is also

00:018:18.000 --> 00:018:25.000
a general charity called Sadaqa and this is an on-the-spot charity. You're

00:018:25.000 --> 00:018:28.000
walking in the street and you see a poor person and you want to help, then you

00:018:28.000 --> 00:018:33.000
help that person and this is called Sadaqa or charity. You're supposed to be

00:018:33.000 --> 00:018:38.000
charitable the whole year, all the time. You must be charitable. But the ZAKAT

00:018:38.000 --> 00:018:44.000
is the obligatory charity where you give it to someone you personally know.

00:018:44.000 --> 00:018:53.000
You personally know that this fellow is poor and needs help and you give your 2.5%

00:018:53.000 --> 00:018:56.000
to these people that you personally know. You cannot consider

00:018:56.000 --> 00:019:02.000
the taxes, for example, as ZAKAT charity, because you don't know where the taxes

00:019:02.000 --> 00:019:06.000
will go. They can go to fix the street or something, or to the army or something.

00:019:06.000 --> 00:019:11.000
But the idea behind ZAKAT is that you give it to the people that you

00:019:11.000 --> 00:019:17.000
personally know are in need. And the Quran, as I said, lists the parents first,

00:019:17.000 --> 00:019:23.000
the relatives, your own - you start with your own people then you go to

00:019:23.000 --> 00:019:26.000
other strangers in that order.

00:019:27.000 --> 00:019:33.000
The fourth pillar of Islam is Zakat charity.

00:019:33.000 --> 00:019:46.000
Zakat is obligatory once a year and is 2.5% of your net worth at the time..

00:019:46.000 --> 00:019:56.000
Quran specifies the recipients as people you know, beginning with your parents

00:020:00.000 --> 00:020:08.000
The fifth pillar of Islam is Hajj pilgrimage to the Holy Land in Mecca.

00:020:08.000 --> 00:020:13.000
And this is only, of course, for the people who can afford it. When you can

00:020:13.000 --> 00:020:19.000
afford it, you go to Mecca and you observe Hajj, and this is commemoration of

00:020:19.000 --> 00:020:27.000
the prophet Abraham, not the man Abraham but his

00:020:27.000 --> 00:020:34.000
exemplary submission to God. He thought... he saw a dream one time and he thought

00:020:34.000 --> 00:020:38.000
that God was commanding him to sacrifice his only son, Ismail.

00:020:38.000 --> 00:020:43.000
And he proceeded to carry out this command even though God did not order

00:020:43.000 --> 00:020:49.000
him to do it. He just thought in a dream that God was ordering him to do it. But he was

00:020:49.000 --> 00:020:53.000
willing to sacrifice his own son in submission to God, and of course, God

00:020:53.000 --> 00:021:01.000
intervened to save Ismail and Abraham from this tragedy. And God

00:021:01.000 --> 00:021:07.000
substituted a sheep to be sacrificed instead of Ismail. And this is what you

00:021:07.000 --> 00:021:12.000
do when you go to Hajj. So, and Hajj consists of arriving in Mecca dressed

00:021:12.000 --> 00:021:17.000
only in untailored clothes, just a sheet or something.

00:021:17.000 --> 00:021:23.000
and seamless shoes or sandals, seamless

00:021:23.000 --> 00:021:28.000
clothes and seamless sandal. The women dress in a regular dress that is

00:021:28.000 --> 00:021:31.000
simple. So, you cannot tell the rich from the poor.

00:021:43.000 --> 00:021:56.000
The fifth pillar of Islam is pilgrimage Hajj to Mecca.

00:021:56.000 --> 00:021:58.000
To observe Hajj, you go to

00:021:58.000 --> 00:022:04.000
Mecca dressed in seamless clothes and seamless sandals. This is for the men.

00:022:04.000 --> 00:022:12.000
The women dress modestly in regular modest dress, all white dress, for

00:022:12.000 --> 00:022:18.000
example, so you cannot tell the rich from the poor. You get to Mecca and you go

00:022:18.000 --> 00:022:23.000
around the Ka‘bah in Mecca seven times. Then, you go between Safa and Marwah, the

00:022:23.000 --> 00:022:29.000
knolls of Safa and Marwah seven times. Then, you go to 'Arafat, Mount 'Arafat and you

00:022:29.000 --> 00:022:35.000
stand there the whole day, which is the 10th day of the twelfth, the last month in

00:022:35.000 --> 00:022:40.000
the Islamic calendar. The tenth day of the Hijr. You spend that whole day on

00:022:40.000 --> 00:022:46.000
Mount 'Arafat commemorating God, worshiping and praying. And then, you go to

00:022:46.000 --> 00:022:52.000
Mina, it's a little town near Mecca. You go to Mina for two or three days.

00:022:52.000 --> 00:022:57.000
Then, you go back to the Ka‘bah, go around it seven times, which is called the farewell

00:022:57.000 --> 00:023:03.000
circumambulation around the Ka‘bah, and this is it. Now, my advice to you is

00:023:03.000 --> 00:023:08.000
never to go to Medina because people go to Medina and they ruin their Hajj. They

00:023:08.000 --> 00:023:12.000
